spans.s:
आ-नत, अस्, आ, अम्, bending, stooping, bowed;
pacified, conciliated; humbled; submissive, obedient;
saluted reverently.
—आनत-ज, आस्, m. pl. a class of
divine beings.

अननुभाषण अन्-अनुभाषण, अम्, n. not
repeating (for the sake of challenging) a proposition;
tacit assent.

अन्-अपराध, अस्, m. innocence, innocuousness;
(अस्, आ, अम्), innocent, faultless; free from defects.
—अनपराध-त्व, अम्, n. freedom from fault.

अनपाय अन्-अपाय, अस्, आ, अम्, free from
loss, undiminished; not passing away, imperishable;
(अस्), m. freedom from loss or from wear and tear;
permanence, imperishable nature; epithet of Śiva.

अनाप्त अन्-आप्त, अस्, आ, अम्, unattained, un-
obtained; unsuccessful in the effort to attain or obtain;
not apt, unfit; (अस्), m. a stranger.

अनर्ह अन्-अर्ह, अस्, आ, अम्, or अन्-अर्हत्, अन्,
अन्ती, अत्, undeserving of punishment or of reward;
unworthy; inadequate, unsuitable.

अन्-अवसित, अस्, आ, अम्, not set, not terminated;
(आ), f., N. of a species of the Triṣṭubh metre, con-
sisting of four lines with eleven feet in each.

अनवेक्ष अन्-अवेक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, regardless;
(अम्), ind. irrespectively; without regard to; (आ), f.
or अन्-अवेक्षण, अम्, n. regardlessness.

अन्-आगामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, not coming, not arriving;
not future, not subject to returning; (ई), m. epithet
of the third among the four Buddhist orders.

अनालम्ब अन्-आलम्ब, अस्, आ, अम्, unsupported,
without stay or support; (अस्), m. want of support;
despondency.

आनन्द् आ-नन्द्, cl. 1. P. -नन्दति, -दितुम्,
to rejoice: Caus. P. -नन्दयति, -यितुम्, to gladden;
A. to amuse one's self.
